# SABOTAGE: D7 (ADR-046 §4.6) — the Csv.compact/1 guard clause for a nested
# %Samen.Masked{} is removed, so the generic struct clause below unwraps it via
# Map.from_struct/1 and a container-nested masked value serializes as
# {"token":"vt_…","label":…} — leaking the vault token into a CSV cell, defeating
# the module's "NEVER a vt_* token" guarantee. The D7 proof flips: the RED
# assertions (masked cell, no vt_ token) fail because the nested masked now
# serializes its vt_ token instead of ••••. INV-1 preserved by the FIX; this
# sabotage only proves the guard is load-bearing (its removal reintroduces the leak).
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/csv_nested_masking_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: nested inside a MAP
# MUST_FAIL: nested inside a LIST
# MUST_FAIL: nested DEEPLY
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/csv.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/csv.ex
index 8c1ca84..f64b89b 100644
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/csv.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/csv.ex
@@ -288,16 +288,6 @@ defmodule Samen.Web.Csv do
     [second: seconds] |> Duration.new!() |> Duration.to_iso8601()
   end
 
-  # D7 / ADR-046 §4.6 — a %Masked{} nested INSIDE a container cell (a `:map`/list
-  # column value) must serialize as its MASKED representation (`••••` via its own
-  # Jason.Encoder), NEVER unwrapped to its `vt_*` token. Without this clause the
-  # generic struct clause below would `Map.from_struct/1` it into
-  # `{"token":"vt_…","label":…}`, defeating the module's "NEVER a vt_* token"
-  # guarantee for any nested occurrence. Kept BEFORE the generic struct clause so
-  # the masked wrapper is preserved (Jason then renders it `••••`). The top-level
-  # `cell(%Samen.Masked{})` clause already covers the direct (non-nested) case.
-  defp compact(%Samen.Masked{} = masked), do: masked
-
   defp compact(%_{} = struct), do: struct |> Map.from_struct() |> compact()
 
   defp compact(%{} = map),
